From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LeavesMC <noreply@leavesmc.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] FerriteCore blockstate and component memory

FerriteCore contributes two allocation reductions that still apply to this tree,
reworked so that nothing depends on mixin accessors, reflection, or on writing
`final` fields after the values were already published.

1. Block state cache deduplication. Every `BlockBehaviour.Cache` used to hold
   its own `collisionShape` (usually an `ArrayVoxelShape`) plus a freshly
   allocated `boolean[12]` for `faceSturdy`. Both are now normalised inside the
   `Cache` constructor, before they reach their `final` fields, so block states
   with equivalent geometry share a single instance. Only `ArrayVoxelShape` is
   considered; `CubeVoxelShape` and `SliceShape` pass through untouched. The
   containers are guarded by `synchronized` because `Blocks.<clinit>` builds
   caches from several threads. Upstream's `replaceInternals` step is
   deliberately not ported: Paper's Moonrise derives and caches fourteen fields
   at the end of every concrete `VoxelShape` constructor, so rewriting the
   coordinate arrays afterwards would leave stale cached data behind.

2. Empty data component patch singleton. A `PatchedDataComponentMap` that ends
   up without overrides keeps an empty `Reference2ObjectArrayMap` alive; it is
   handed back to the immutable empty map instead. This is mutually exclusive
   with `performance.sleeping-block-entity`, which keys off the `copyOnWrite`
   epoch transitions the shrink would introduce.

Both parts are off by default (`performance.ferrite-blockstate-dedup` and
`performance.ferrite-component-patch-shrink`); with the options disabled the
original expressions are evaluated unchanged.

This patch is Powered by FerriteCore(https://github.com/malte0811/FerriteCore)

This patch is based on the following mixins:
* "malte0811/ferritecore/mixin/blockstatecache/BlockStateCacheMixin.java"
* "malte0811/ferritecore/mixin/datacomponents/PatchedDataComponentMapMixin.java"
By: malte0811
As part of: FerriteCore (https://github.com/malte0811/FerriteCore)
Licensed under: MIT (https://github.com/malte0811/FerriteCore/blob/master/LICENSE)

Modules of the mod that are not ported: neighbour table compaction and property
table compaction (already superseded by Paper's `ZeroCollidingReferenceStateTable`
and by `StateHolder#moonrise$init`, which drops the tables at the end of
registration), and the threading detector rewrite (the `PalettedContainer` field
it targeted no longer exists in this tree).

diff --git a/net/minecraft/core/component/PatchedDataComponentMap.java b/net/minecraft/core/component/PatchedDataComponentMap.java
index e33160945fefd7bc7fb0ea44104b2dfe2f43a3d3..b8dafb2920b717d429589d1470fcb6b91faff029 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/core/component/PatchedDataComponentMap.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/core/component/PatchedDataComponentMap.java
@@ -54,6 +54,25 @@ public final class PatchedDataComponentMap implements DataComponentMap, org.leav
         return true;
     }
 
+    // Leaves start - FerriteCore component patch shrink
+    /**
+     * Replaces an emptied patch with the immutable singleton, so objects that never keep a non-default component stop
+     * holding on to an (empty) {@code Reference2ObjectArrayMap}. The {@code copyOnWrite} flag is restored alongside it,
+     * keeping the invariant "immutable empty patch implies copyOnWrite" intact.
+     *
+     * <p>Deliberately inert while Lithium's sleeping block entity tracking is enabled: that feature keys off
+     * {@code copyOnWrite} epochs, and the extra epochs introduced here would wake sleeping block entities needlessly.</p>
+     */
+    private void ferriteShrinkIfEmpty() {
+        if (org.snowballmc.snowball.LeavesConfig.performance.ferriteComponentPatchShrink
+            && !org.snowballmc.snowball.LeavesConfig.performance.sleepingBlockEntity
+            && this.patch.isEmpty()) {
+            this.patch = Reference2ObjectMaps.emptyMap();
+            this.copyOnWrite = true;
+        }
+    }
+    // Leaves end - FerriteCore component patch shrink
+
     @Override
     public <T> @Nullable T get(final DataComponentType<? extends T> type) {
         return DataComponentPatch.getFromPatchAndPrototype(this.patch, this.prototype, type);
@@ -72,6 +91,7 @@ public final class PatchedDataComponentMap implements DataComponentMap, org.leav
         } else {
             lastValue = this.patch.put(type, Removed.nullToRemoved(value));
         }
+        this.ferriteShrinkIfEmpty(); // Leaves - FerriteCore component patch shrink
 
         return lastValue != null ? Objects.requireNonNullElse((T)Removed.removedToNull(lastValue), defaultValue) : defaultValue;
     }
@@ -89,6 +109,7 @@ public final class PatchedDataComponentMap implements DataComponentMap, org.leav
         } else {
             lastValue = this.patch.remove(type);
         }
+        this.ferriteShrinkIfEmpty(); // Leaves - FerriteCore component patch shrink
 
         return (T)(lastValue != null ? Removed.removedToNull(lastValue) : defaultValue);
     }
@@ -99,6 +120,7 @@ public final class PatchedDataComponentMap implements DataComponentMap, org.leav
         for (Entry<DataComponentType<?>, Object> entry : Reference2ObjectMaps.fastIterable(patch.map)) {
             this.applyPatch(entry.getKey(), entry.getValue());
         }
+        this.ferriteShrinkIfEmpty(); // Leaves - FerriteCore component patch shrink
     }
 
     private void applyPatch(final DataComponentType<?> type, final Object value) {
@@ -120,11 +142,13 @@ public final class PatchedDataComponentMap implements DataComponentMap, org.leav
         this.ensureMapOwnership();
         this.patch.clear();
         this.patch.putAll(patch.map);
+        this.ferriteShrinkIfEmpty(); // Leaves - FerriteCore component patch shrink
     }
 
     public void clearPatch() {
         this.ensureMapOwnership();
         this.patch.clear();
+        this.ferriteShrinkIfEmpty(); // Leaves - FerriteCore component patch shrink
     }
 
     public void setAll(final DataComponentMap components) {
